        "complete": true,
        "reason": null,
        "diff": "--- /dev/null\n+++ /home/agent/workspace/obligations.txt\n@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@\n+Proof Obligations for claim.txt / spec.txt\n+==========================================\n+Spec:  forall x : Int. (x + 1) * (x - 1) = x * x - 1\n+\n+OB-1 [Well-formedness]\n+  The specification is a well-typed first-order formula.\n+  Show: x : Int implies (x + 1), (x - 1), (x * x - 1) : Int and the\n+  equality (x + 1) * (x - 1) = x * x - 1 is well-formed.\n+\n+OB-2 [Main goal]\n+  forall x : Int. (x + 1) * (x - 1) = x * x - 1\n+  Prove the universal statement for an arbitrary integer x.\n+\n+OB-3 [Ring expansion]\n+  For arbitrary x : Int, expand the product using distributivity.\n+  Show: (x + 1) * (x - 1) = x * x - x + x - 1\n+\n+OB-4 [Additive cancellation]\n+  For arbitrary x : Int, simplify the expansion.\n+  Show: x * x - x + x - 1 = x * x - 1\n+  Depends on: x - x = 0 and y + 0 = y (additive inverse and identity).\n+\n+OB-5 [Axiom side conditions]\n+  OB-3 and OB-4 rely on the ring axioms of the integers\n+  (associativity, commutativity, distributivity, additive inverse,\n+  additive identity). Discharge by citing the standard axiomatization\n+  of Int, or prove them if the axioms are not assumed.\n+\n+Discharge order: OB-1, then OB-5 (assumed or proven), then OB-3, OB-4,\n+which together discharge OB-2.\n"
